# The rules a generated build uses when the project has no .dockerignore.
# The engine writes them into panelalpha.Dockerfile.dockerignore, which
# BuildKit reads instead of .dockerignore, together with .git and the engine's
# own files; see BuildContextIgnore. A project's .dockerignore is never edited.
#
# .git is the load-bearing line. Two clones of one repository give an
# identical worktree and different .git bytes, so leaving it in the build
# context made `COPY . .` hash differently on every deploy and rebuilt every
# layer below it.
.git
node_modules
.panelalpha
npm-debug.log
